# Calculator Automation Example: Simple Calculation
# This example demonstrates basic automation with Calculator app
#
# Prerequisites:
# - macOS Calculator app (pre-installed on macOS)
# - Accessibility permission granted to Terminal
#
# What this script does:
# 1. Launches Calculator
# 2. Performs calculation: 7 + 3 = 10
# 3. Copies result to clipboard
# 4. Clears and performs: 5 × 4 = 20
#
# This is a good starting example because:
# - Calculator is always available on macOS
# - No need to install Excel or other software
# - Quick to test (runs in ~10 seconds)

mode continue

log === Calculator Simple Automation ===

# Step 1: Launch Calculator
log Step 1: Launching Calculator
launch Calculator
wait 2

# Step 2: Perform first calculation (7 + 3)
log Step 2: Calculating 7 + 3
find 7
click
wait 0.3

find Add
click
wait 0.3

find 3
click
wait 0.3

find Equals
click
wait 0.5

log Result: 10

# Step 3: Copy result to clipboard
log Step 3: Copying result to clipboard
pressKey Cmd+C
wait 0.5

# Step 4: Clear and perform second calculation (5 × 4)
log Step 4: Clearing and calculating 5 × 4
find Clear
click
wait 0.5

find 5
click
wait 0.3

find Multiply
click
wait 0.3

find 4
click
wait 0.3

find Equals
click
wait 0.5

log Result: 20

# Step 5: Demonstrate keyboard shortcuts
log Step 5: Testing keyboard shortcut (Cmd+C for copy)
pressKey Cmd+C
wait 0.3

log
log === Calculator Automation Complete! ===
log
log Performed operations:
log   - 7 + 3 = 10
log   - 5 × 4 = 20
log   - Copied results to clipboard
